{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 44, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3.5-122b-a10b", "content": "**Chasing Cherry Blossoms: A Weekend in Kyoto**\n\nStepping off the bullet train in Kyoto felt like entering a different era. The air was crisp, carrying the faint, sweet scent of blooming cherry blossoms that marked the start of spring. Our journey began at Fushimi Inari Taisha, where thousands of vibrant vermilion torii gates created a mesmerizing tunnel winding up the sacred mountain. Walking through them felt spiritual, a rhythmic meditation of footsteps against stone.\n\nLater, we wandered into the Arashiyama Bamboo Grove. Towering stalks swayed gently, creating a hauntingly beautiful natural symphony that echoed through the forest. It was a stark, serene contrast to the bustling city streets we had left behind.\n\nNo trip to Japan is complete without the culinary experience. We dined at a tiny ramen shop tucked away in a narrow alley. The broth was rich and complex, simmered for hours, while the noodles had the perfect chew. Sharing a bowl of fresh sushi at the Nishiki Market was equally unforgettable; the fish was so fresh it seemed to melt on the tongue.\n\nAs evening fell, we visited the Gion district. The wooden machiya houses glowed under paper lanterns, and for a fleeting moment, we spotted a Geisha hurrying to an appointment. The blend of ancient tradition and modern life is what makes Japan so captivating. Every corner revealed a new story, from the quiet temples to the neon-lit convenience stores.\n\nThis short trip was just a glimpse, but it left an indelible mark. Japan doesn't just welcome visitors; it invites you to experience a world where the past and future dance together in perfect harmony. I am already dreaming of my next return.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.29092026}, {"token": "Ch", "logprob": -0.41426665}, {"token": "asing", "logprob": -1.5019732}, {"token": " Cherry", "logprob": -0.013413402}, {"token": " Bloss"